WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.713
What must not change proves
as much as what does.

2
00:00:02.713 --> 00:00:04.976
The laptop's device groups stay put,

3
00:00:04.976 --> 00:00:08.412
because device rules can't
read the user's attributes.

4
00:00:08.412 --> 00:00:13.188
The service principal the analyst
sponsors still records the analyst's key,

5
00:00:13.188 --> 00:00:16.600
and a sponsor's own move
belongs to the non-person track.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.275
Nothing is assigned by hand.

7
00:00:18.275 --> 00:00:20.675
Then the proof, owned by the CISO.

8
00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:23.387
Run the drift scan; it
should find nothing.

9
00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:27.575
Rerun the kit with the earlier
snapshot and a fresh HR export.

10
00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:32.110
The membership check should show exactly
the expected changes and no others,

11
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:36.361
the counts per organization code should
reconcile with HR, and the mover

12
00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:40.612
workflow's own run history should show
it ran for this user and what it did.

13
00:00:40.612 --> 00:00:43.952
The leaver-and-hire timeliness
check doesn't prove that,

14
00:00:43.952 --> 00:00:46.712
because it reads hire
and leave triggers only.

15
00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:49.291
Rollback is the simplest of any gate:

16
00:00:49.291 --> 00:00:54.362
reverse the personnel action in HR
and let the same path undo the access.

17
00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:56.570
Never fix the directory by hand.
